# GET / — serve the page from a gated op, not a static FILES/index.html.
#
# Static files bypass the txcl pipeline (and so the auth gate in 090/095), so a
# static index.html would be world-readable and — worse — would load without the
# browser ever prompting for the password, leaving a legit user unable to sign
# in (a fetch/WebSocket 401 does not trigger the Basic-auth dialog; only a
# top-level 401 does). Serving the page HERE puts it behind the gate: an
# unauthenticated GET / gets 401 from 095, the browser prompts, and the cached
# credentials then flow to the /screen WebSocket and the fetch() calls. The HTML
# is base64-embedded (@web.res.body is base64); there is no public copy.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/"
  EMIT @web.res.status = 200,
       @web.res.headers.content-type.0 = "text/html; charset=utf-8",
       @web.res.body = ""
